## Progress

- **12:45** First working layout. Placement is done one window at a time —
  each terminal spawned with its own `--app-id`, polled for in the sway tree,
  then explicitly focused before splitting off the next. Brave is launched
  into a throwaway holder pane and swapped into its slot once its window
  appears, so its slow startup cannot scramble the tree.
- **12:47** Bug: the 40/60 split kept coming out inverted. `focus` and
  `resize` sent as two separate `swaymsg` calls are not atomic and brave
  grabbed focus in between, so the resize hit the browser. All geometry
  commands now carry `[con_id=…]` criteria instead of relying on focus.
- **12:47** Self-inflicted: a runtime `for_window [class="…"]` rule for beeper
  matched native Wayland windows (which have no X11 class) and vacuumed
  workspace 1 into the scratchpad. Reverted, workspace restored to its exact
  original tabbed layout, and the permanent rule in the sway config matches on
  `app_id` only.
- **12:49** Repo created at ~/ŻYCIE/VIBECODING/go-layout, pushed public.
  ~/.local/bin/go-layout symlinked into it so edits are live.
- **13:10** `--fresh` made the default: build on the lowest empty workspace
  rather than always workspace 1, since on an occupied tabbed workspace the
  whole layout nested itself into a single new tab. Surfaced two more bugs —
  a second `go` latched onto the first run's `go-r1` (app_ids now tagged with
  the run's PID), and brave activating an old window dragged focus back to
  the wrong workspace (focus is now claimed last).
- **13:30** `go` did nothing at all in a real terminal — three silent
  failures stacked: `setsid -f` lost the race against the terminal closing
  and was killed before executing a line; `swaymsg exec go-layout` found
  nothing because sway's PATH has no ~/.local/bin, and reported success
  anyway; and the closing terminal dragged focus back after the workspace
  switch. Launcher now goes through sway with an absolute path, and the
  script asserts the workspace switch and moves the anchor pane if sway put
  it elsewhere. Logging switched to per-line append so a killed run leaves a
  trace instead of vanishing.
- **14:09** Verified beeper end to end, both launched by `go` and launched
  independently: parked in the scratchpad at 1200x800 either way, no loose
  window on any workspace.

- **15:00** SoundVisualizer session begins. Tyto moved to the Pi; enabled it in
  `config.toml` on the stable by-id path and copied the corrected
  `cal_thrust = -1.0019910071` across from the documented value. Mics came up
  10 of 11 — the missing one was absent at USB level, the documented
  power-but-not-data USB-C symptom. Reseated, then found SoundVis still showed
  10: PortAudio enumerates once at startup, so the server needed a restart.
- **15:20** Pi overlay work. Both research trees lived on the overlay rootfs,
  so every tree edit was silently lost on reboot — moved to
  `/home/pi/data/research-trees/` and symlinked, matching how measurements and
  config.toml already work. Verified across a full reboot cycle.
  `raspi-config nonint do_overlayfs` turned out to be a **no-op on this Pi**:
  it drives an initramfs `boot=overlay` mechanism while the machine runs the
  overlayroot package off the kernel cmdline. It exits 0 and changes nothing.
  CLAUDE.md corrected — the real toggle is a sed on
  `/boot/firmware/cmdline.txt`, and `:recurse=0` must never be dropped.
- **15:35** Mic d unbindable. The preset wanted port paths `1-1.2` and `1-1.3`
  that the udev rules no longer covered (regenerated once while two mics were
  unplugged). Regenerated the rules, which fixed mic c; mic d had physically
  moved to `3-1.1`, confirmed by the serial printed on the mic body (8112310)
  before re-binding, since every UMIK-2 reports USB serial `00000` and software
  cannot tell them apart. Also found `MicList`'s reconcile effect wipes
  `deviceIndex` on every render when the row's `alsaCardId` is stale, so
  re-picking the device was the only escape.
- **16:00** Baseline captured twice before it was right: first run had a dead
  motor (ESC never armed — current ~0 A at every step, caught by comparing
  telemetry across runs), second was missing mic d. Third run clean.
- **16:15** Overlay labels: two series rendered identically as "6in · 2000µs"
  because the label was built from propeller + shroud only and ignored `notes`,
  which is the only field distinguishing two baselines of the same motor and
  prop. Fixed — then found the compare-config dropdown builds its own label
  independently and needed the same fix.
- **16:30** The expensive bug: `ResearchTreeNodePicker` only autofilled *empty*
  fields, so switching to a different node left the previous node's shroud and
  notes in place — and since the key is `motor__propeller__shroud__notes`, the
  felt capture was stored under the cork key. Only caught by reading the stored
  data. Now a field is replaced when it is empty **or** still equal to what the
  previously picked node put there; hand-typed values are still left alone.
- **17:00** All four material runs also landed under a typo'd `f2004` motor —
  a free-text field the picker never touches. Renamed each key in place
  (directory + `key.json`) rather than re-running the motor.
- **18:39** Campaign complete. Data pushed to `SoundVisualizer-data` @
  `acb4016`, 10 keys, 0 unpushed. Research tree updated with links and
  statuses. Issue #10 filed for Paweł to upload the set to the server. Pi
  powered down cleanly.

